<PageLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description="How Ruta y Ritmo chooses, writes and corrects its content."
  crumb="Editorial policy"
>
  <p><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> 20 October 2026.</p>

  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>
    Ruta y Ritmo publishes training, route, gear, nutrition, health and race guides for
    everyday runners. The goal is that you can use what you read: a plan you understand,
    a route you can follow or a sign that tells you when to stop.
  </p>

  <h2>Sources and accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    The content draws on public sources: health bodies, federations, technical guides
    and cited studies. Estimates are presented as estimates and opinions are identified
    as opinions.
  </p>

  <h2>AI tools</h2>
  <p>
    Some texts are produced with the support of AI tools and checked against public
    sources. They are not presented as personal experience or professional advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Health and nutrition</h2>
  <p>
    Health and nutrition articles are informative and do not replace an individual
    consultation. No cures, miracle diets or guaranteed results are promised. When there
    are warning signs, the article says to stop and see a professional.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Advertising does not decide what gets published. Ad spaces are separated from the
    content and labelled. Affiliate links are marked according to the
    <a href="/en/afiliados/">affiliate disclosure</a>. We do not accept payment for
    positive reviews.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you find an error, email
    <a href="mailto:hola@rutayritmo.com">hola@rutayritmo.com</a> with the link and the
    detail you believe is wrong. If it is confirmed, it will be corrected and the article
    date will be updated.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    Gear and route articles are reviewed when the product, the route or the practical
    information changes. The update date appears at the top of the article.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
